 "note": "Cases for test_contract_book (bookOpsLikePython): the book and page ops of M4 (Python's ops._apply_one with pagespec.py, bookops.py and merge.py: set_page_spec, set_spread, add_cover, for_pages, set_assignee, import_pages) on the book `pyref_harness.py make-pagesbook` makes (the op book: six pages, page 5 held by ai:other, a front cover as page 7; with briefs' regions, 3D guides, effect lines, an old tone's region, a mask and a hand-drawn balloon besides). $OTHER is the book it makes to take pages from (five pages: three, a back cover and a jacket), $PAGESBOOK the book itself on disk, $LEGACY the legacy books of data/legacy, $SCRATCH the books the test makes that cannot be read (nowhere, empty, broken JSON, newer, notbook, damaged: a picture missing) and areas (the other book with areas kept on its page 2 that name its layers). The format is ops_cases.json's; cpp: the code this build refuses the case with where Python keeps what it cannot hold (a paper or margins that are not finite numbers, a paint layer moved onto a basic frame of no finite size), goes on with a paper too large to hold a page's pixels, reads a book this build would open read-only (damaged), or words a refusal its own way (a newer version, JSON that is not a book: Python stops with a traceback), and cpp_says: words of that refusal; or cpp \"deviates\": a case this build answers otherwise than Python on purpose, the user's decision cpp_says names (D1: set_page_spec puts each page's pixels on its own paper, a cover's too, and moves a layer's mask with what it masks; D2: import_pages and duplicate_page point what names a layer on a page taken in or copied at its new layers), Python's but at the places cpp_differs lists (paths into the step's reply, full snapshot and payload; * any key or index), keeping what cpp_keeps says (opsupport.hpp kept_by_deviation) after the case and saved and read back, where Python's book does not. New ids count from first_id (0x1000).",
